WEBVTT

00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:09.535
Woody, you did all you could.

00:00:09.735 --> 00:00:11.375
Time to go home.

00:00:11.535 --> 00:00:12.615
No.

00:00:12.735 --> 00:00:13.735
Woody.

00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:15.175
I don't leave toys behind,
Buzz.

00:00:15.255 --> 00:00:16.615
Yeah, but, Woody,
you're actually leaving...

00:00:16.695 --> 00:00:18.535
Not now. Not ever.

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:22.135
And he left me behind.

00:00:23.095 --> 00:00:24.735
(SIGHS) What now, inner voice?

00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:26.655
VOICE BOX: Mission
accomplished. Return to base.

00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:29.015
Go back to the RV?
What about Woody?

00:00:29.175 --> 00:00:30.895
VOICE BOX: We're going home,
space ranger.

00:00:31.055 --> 00:00:32.295
Fall back, this planet...

00:00:32.455 --> 00:00:33.495
Retreat! There's too...

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:35.495
Go! Time to fly! Exit the...
Back... Run...

00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:37.335
Get out!
Returning to Star Command.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:39.735
Okay. Okay.

00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:41.295
(SIGHS)

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.215
Thanks a lot, inner voice.

00:00:44.415 --> 00:00:47.935
Harmony, honey, help Grandma
close up for the night.

00:00:48.095 --> 00:00:50.855
HARMONY: Okay. Then can we
go to the carnival?

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:52.015
MARGARET: Sure.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:58.775
-Ahhh!
-GABBY GABBY: Hello, Woody.

00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:01.495
I knew you'd be back.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.175
You don't know me.

00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:05.895
But I do.

00:01:06.495 --> 00:01:09.495
You were left in the closet,
feeling useless...

00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:12.095
wondering if you'll
ever get played with.

00:01:12.295 --> 00:01:14.055
I'm not leaving without Forky.

00:01:14.295 --> 00:01:16.295
Can we agree
on just one thing?

00:01:17.015 --> 00:01:18.175
What?

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:19.975
That being there for a child

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:23.375
is the most noble thing
a toy can do.

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:25.975
Okay.

00:01:28.295 --> 00:01:31.855
I was defective
right out of the box.

00:01:32.015 --> 00:01:34.815
I can only imagine what it
must have been like for you.

00:01:36.455 --> 00:01:39.375
All that time you spent
with Andy...

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:43.335
riding a bike with him
for the first time...

00:01:44.095 --> 00:01:47.175
comforting him
when he skinned his knee...

00:01:47.655 --> 00:01:49.615
proudly watching him grow up.

00:01:51.015 --> 00:01:53.975
And then you got
a second chance with Bonnie...

00:01:54.135 --> 00:01:56.855
giving her comfort
when she's scared at school...

00:01:57.015 --> 00:01:59.615
helping her
when she needs it most.

00:02:00.695 --> 00:02:04.335
You've been there through
all their ups and downs.

00:02:06.295 --> 00:02:07.775
Please.

00:02:07.975 --> 00:02:09.175
Be honest with me.

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.855
Was it as wonderful
as it sounds?

00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:19.135
It was.

00:02:22.655 --> 00:02:26.735
All I want is a chance
for just one of those moments.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.935
I'd give anything to be loved
the way you have.

00:02:38.975 --> 00:02:40.415
Just leave me Forky.

00:02:42.135 --> 00:02:43.775
Bonnie needs him.

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.055
Of course.

00:02:53.655 --> 00:02:55.895
(BONNIE'S DAD GRUNTING)

00:02:58.215 --> 00:03:00.935
(LAUGHS)
The flat tire is fixed!

00:03:01.095 --> 00:03:02.935
Come on, Woody, hurry up.

00:03:03.095 --> 00:03:05.375
-Where is he?
-(ALL GASP)

00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:07.215
JESSIE: Buzz!
HAMM: Buzz!

00:03:07.415 --> 00:03:08.775
DOLLY: Where's Woody?
HAMM: And Forky?

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.935
We have a situation.

00:03:10.095 --> 00:03:11.695
They need to be extracted
from the antique store.

00:03:11.855 --> 00:03:13.175
-How do we do that?
-(DOOR OPENS)

00:03:13.255 --> 00:03:14.935
BONNIE'S DAD: Okay, let's
make sure we have everything.

00:03:15.015 --> 00:03:16.695
BONNIE'S MOM: (SIGHS) Finally.

00:03:16.855 --> 00:03:18.255
It's okay.
Any minute now...

00:03:18.415 --> 00:03:20.735
Bonnie will notice
her backpack is missing.

00:03:20.895 --> 00:03:22.695
She'll realize she left it
at the antique store...

00:03:22.855 --> 00:03:24.215
and we'll head back in there.

00:03:24.615 --> 00:03:26.215
BONNIE'S MOM: Okay.
Looks like we have everything.

00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:27.775
-You good, Bonnie?
-Yup.

00:03:27.855 --> 00:03:29.095
BONNIE'S DAD:
Great. Let's get out of here.

00:03:29.455 --> 00:03:30.495
(ENGINE STARTS)

00:03:30.575 --> 00:03:32.415
Okay, genius,
what do we do now?

00:03:32.495 --> 00:03:33.495
BUZZ: Hmm.

00:03:33.575 --> 00:03:34.575
VOICE BOX:
Scanning perimeter.

00:03:34.655 --> 00:03:35.655
Laser at full power!

00:03:35.735 --> 00:03:37.895
-Buzz, what are you doing?
-I'm thinking.

00:03:37.975 --> 00:03:39.655
BONNIE'S DAD: Honey, will you
please shut that toy off?

00:03:39.775 --> 00:03:40.775
Yeah, I got it.

00:03:40.855 --> 00:03:42.775
VOICE BOX: Attack!
Meteor shower! Look out!

00:03:42.935 --> 00:03:45.495
It's a secret mission in
uncharted space! Let's go!

00:03:45.695 --> 00:03:47.935
Buzz Lightyear to the rescue!

00:03:48.095 --> 00:03:49.215
Bonnie,
how do you turn this off?

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.295
VOICE BOX: Full speed ahead!

00:03:50.495 --> 00:03:52.215
-Open the pod bay doors!
-BONNIE: I don't know.

00:03:52.295 --> 00:03:53.855
It's just you and me now,
cadet.

00:03:53.935 --> 00:03:55.255
A distress signal is coming
from that rocket.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:56.535
BONNIE'S DAD:
Just toss it in the drawer.

00:03:56.935 --> 00:03:59.975
VOICE BOX:
To infinity and beyond!

00:04:00.055 --> 00:04:02.375
Uh-oh. Uh, your backpack's in
the antique store! Let's go!

00:04:02.535 --> 00:04:03.815
Oh, no, my backpack!

00:04:04.855 --> 00:04:07.135
I left my backpack
in the antique store!

00:04:07.215 --> 00:04:08.535
-(BONNIE'S DAD SIGHS)
-You did?

00:04:08.695 --> 00:04:11.615
All right,
let's swing by and get it.

00:04:13.575 --> 00:04:15.575
(CHILDREN CHATTERING
EXCITEDLY)

00:04:16.615 --> 00:04:19.495
Ugh! I can't believe
the nerve of that cowboy.

00:04:19.575 --> 00:04:20.935
I mean,
who does he think he is?

00:04:21.015 --> 00:04:22.295
-(BLEATS)
-Exactly!

00:04:22.375 --> 00:04:24.055
He was way out of line.

00:04:24.215 --> 00:04:25.895
You did the right thing
leaving him behind.

00:04:25.975 --> 00:04:27.255
(BLEATING)

00:04:27.335 --> 00:04:28.815
-Hey, Lamb Chops?
-BO PEEP: Hmm.

00:04:28.895 --> 00:04:30.615
-Coast is clear.
-Oh.

00:04:36.055 --> 00:04:37.055
Head to the middle.

00:04:37.255 --> 00:04:38.655
When the carnival
leaves tomorrow,

00:04:38.735 --> 00:04:39.975
we'll hide right there.

00:04:40.055 --> 00:04:41.295
(RATTLING)

00:04:42.135 --> 00:04:43.335
-Uh, no way!
-Stuff that.

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:44.415
Awesome.

00:04:44.575 --> 00:04:45.775
Stick with me.
You'll be fine.

00:04:45.935 --> 00:04:46.935
-Ready?
-BUNNY AND DUCKY: No!

00:04:47.015 --> 00:04:48.055
And another thing,

00:04:48.135 --> 00:04:49.615
-Woody asked you for help.
-On your mark...

00:04:49.695 --> 00:04:50.735
GIGGLE:
And he treats you like that?

00:04:50.815 --> 00:04:52.975
-...get set...
-He only cares about himself.

00:04:53.055 --> 00:04:54.055
-No!
-(BOTH GRUNT)

00:04:54.135 --> 00:04:55.295
-(BOTH SCREAMING)
-You're wrong.

00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:57.095
Woody's always trying to
do right by his kid.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:58.975
By putting everyone in danger.

00:04:59.055 --> 00:05:01.455
Ugh. That kind of crazy
loyalty just...

00:05:01.655 --> 00:05:02.895
You gotta love him for it.

00:05:03.055 --> 00:05:04.815
-Whoa, say what now?
-(BOTH CONTINUE SCREAMING)

00:05:04.895 --> 00:05:06.335
Hey, hey, hey, Bo!
What's the plan?

00:05:06.415 --> 00:05:07.655
Fill me in here.

00:05:11.135 --> 00:05:12.535
-(BOTH CONTINUE SCREAMING)
-(BLEATING)

00:05:12.615 --> 00:05:13.615
(BOTH GRUNT)

00:05:13.695 --> 00:05:14.975
-Get in! We're going back.
-(GROANS)

00:05:15.055 --> 00:05:16.055
We just got here.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.975
You heard Bo!
We're going back!

00:05:18.135 --> 00:05:20.215
Move your plush! Let's ride!

00:05:26.015 --> 00:05:27.015
(WHIRRING)

00:05:27.095 --> 00:05:28.695
WOODY'S VOICE BOX:
You're my favorite...

00:05:28.775 --> 00:05:31.655
(VOICE DISTORTS)

00:05:36.415 --> 00:05:37.495
(GRUNTS)

00:05:39.255 --> 00:05:40.455
(GROANS)

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:42.335
(GROANS)

00:05:42.415 --> 00:05:43.655
-Yay!
-(GASPS)

00:05:43.735 --> 00:05:44.735
(LAUGHS)

00:05:45.135 --> 00:05:46.815
VOICE BOX:
You are my best friend.

00:05:46.895 --> 00:05:48.295
Let's play all day!

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:50.015
Oh, Benson!
Did you hear that?

00:05:50.175 --> 00:05:51.415
Isn't that lovely?

00:05:51.615 --> 00:05:52.695
VOICE BOX: Time for tea.

00:05:52.855 --> 00:05:54.575
Oh, thank you, Woody.
Thank you!

00:05:54.975 --> 00:05:56.295
-(GRUNTS)
-All my dreams

00:05:56.375 --> 00:05:57.575
are coming true
because of you.

00:05:57.655 --> 00:05:58.735
Thank you! Thank you!

00:05:58.815 --> 00:05:59.815
Uh, you're welcome.

00:05:59.895 --> 00:06:00.895
(GABBY GABBY LAUGHS)

00:06:00.975 --> 00:06:03.015
(SIGHS) It's time, Benson.

00:06:03.815 --> 00:06:06.335
Goodbye, Forky.
I'm going to miss our talks.

00:06:06.495 --> 00:06:08.855
Me, too.
Good luck, Gabby.

00:06:09.015 --> 00:06:10.815
Thank you, my little utensil.

00:06:12.255 --> 00:06:14.935
Bye, Gabby!
Goodbye, Benson!

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.055
He is terrifying.

00:06:18.135 --> 00:06:19.255
-(DOOR OPENS)
-(DOORBELL JINGLES)

00:06:19.335 --> 00:06:20.655
-MARGARET: Hello.
-Hi.

00:06:20.775 --> 00:06:21.935
(GASPS) Bonnie?

00:06:22.015 --> 00:06:23.175
MARGARET:
Can I help you with anything?

00:06:23.255 --> 00:06:24.455
Yeah. We called
about the backpack.

00:06:24.535 --> 00:06:26.335
MARGARET: Oh, yes.
I couldn't find it.

00:06:26.855 --> 00:06:28.135
-(WOODY GASPS)
-Feel free to look around.

00:06:28.215 --> 00:06:30.455
-Quick! Before she finds it!
-(PANTING)

00:06:30.535 --> 00:06:31.575
(GASPS)

00:06:33.015 --> 00:06:35.015
Look! There's Harmony.

00:06:38.015 --> 00:06:39.775
VOICE BOX:
You make me so happy!

00:06:39.855 --> 00:06:40.975
Let's be best friends.

00:06:41.935 --> 00:06:43.375
Oh, this is it!

00:06:43.695 --> 00:06:45.295
We're going home, Forky!

00:06:45.975 --> 00:06:46.975
Huh?

00:06:48.015 --> 00:06:49.895
(WHISPERS) Forky! Oh!

00:06:50.815 --> 00:06:53.175
No, no, no. Woody, look!
It's really happening!

